New module core/vad/:
- silero_vad.py: 16kHz float32 PCM wrapper, 1024-sample window,
  single-VAD simplified from route C dual-VAD logic
- silero_vad.onnx: copied from route C
- Singleton with persistent LSTM state, thread-safe lock

worker.py changes:
- import VAD lazy (graceful fallback if onnxruntime missing)
- duplex_ws audio_chunk: detect_chunk(audio_waveform), prob > 0.5
  → override chunk_force_listen = True, log [VAD-D] auto-interrupt
- prepare msg: reset_state() at session start

config.json port reassign (avoid B-cpp conflict):
- cpp_server_port 19080 -> 19090
- gateway_port 8040 -> 8050
- worker_base_port 22440 -> 22450
- data_dir data -> data-d

E2E verified (CLI test, port 22450, Q4_K_M):
- VAD triggers during user speech (prob 0.6-0.99) -> force_listen=True
- silence: VAD doesn t fire -> model speaks normally
- coexists with route C (port 19060) on GB10 121G unified mem

Branch: route-d (forked from master commit 596d1af)
